Subject: [PATCH] Reset H5 controllers after the kernel UART handover

The loader resets after firmware download, then hands the UART to the kernel
which establishes its own H5 link. With the legacy reset-on-close default,
that handover is not followed by a kernel initialization reset.

On RTL8852BS, fresh controller initialization repeatedly broke CMCC directed
LE reconnects with the saved bonds and resolving list intact. A normal adapter
power cycle restored them. The same loader binary with reset-on-init enabled,
disabled and enabled again produced working, failing and working reconnects;
B25 reconnects also passed. Request the existing UART reset-on-init flag for
H5 so the normal kernel initialization sequence starts from a reset controller.

This is a transport initialization change, not a per-remote reconnect retry.
No device names, addresses, keys, sleeps or background reset services are added.

--- a/hciattach.h
+++ b/hciattach.h
@@ -55,6 +55,7 @@
 #define HCI_UART_H4DS	3
 #define HCI_UART_LL	4
 #define HCI_UART_RAW_DEVICE	0
+#define HCI_UART_RESET_ON_INIT	1
 
 extern uint8_t DBG_ON;
 
--- a/hciattach.c
+++ b/hciattach.c
@@ -227,6 +227,14 @@
 	if (raw)
 		flags |= 1 << HCI_UART_RAW_DEVICE;
 
+	/* The download-time reset precedes the kernel's H5 link setup.
+	 * Let the kernel reset the controller after taking over the UART,
+	 * before programming its runtime state. The legacy UART default
+	 * otherwise defers this reset until the first close.
+	 */
+	if (u->proto == HCI_UART_3WIRE)
+		flags |= 1 << HCI_UART_RESET_ON_INIT;
+
 	fd = open(dev, O_RDWR | O_NOCTTY);
 	if (fd < 0) {
 		RS_ERR("Can't open serial port, %d, %s", errno,
